  "body": "Slice 1 of #926, per the maintainer's direction on the issue: every shipped post script is tested against the post binary on a shared set of recorded edge-case intermediate files, with no `camcraft_app` and no toolpath generation in the suites.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`crates/post/tests/script_<stem>.rs`** - one suite per `assets/posts/*.cps` (11). Each is three lines: `post_suite!(\"<stem>.cps\")` generates one `#[test]` per recorded case, so a failure names the post and the case. Each names its script, so #923 (PR #967) selects it on a `.cps` change.\n- **`crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`** - the shared runner: runs `CARGO_BIN_EXE_post` (`--log` for warnings) on `recorded/streams/<case>.cnc` and compares with `recorded/golden/<stem>/<case>.nc` (the released program: exit 0, no warning) or `<case>.refusal` (the named refusal: the counted warnings the in-app gate blocks on, or the error the binary stopped on). `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` records them.\n- **`crates/post/tests/recorded/streams/*.cnc`** - the nine recorded inputs (the post's `.cnc` intermediate: the `.cl` dump carries no tool, spindle, section, thread or probing records).\n- **Staleness guards** - `crates/post/tests/recorded_streams.rs` rebuilds the six cl-built streams (cl `PathBuilder` + `post::dump` + `cnc::serialize`) byte for byte; `crates/app/tests/recorded_post_streams.rs` rebuilds `probe` (`motion::probing::probe_cycle`) and `drill_retract` (`motion::drilling::drill`) - app is the one crate that sees both motion and post, so no new crate edge. The one hand-written stream (`full_circle_raw`) is guarded by \"parses, and the writer gives back the same text, and it holds its 360-degree record\". The post guard also fails when a shipped `.cps` has no suite, when the stream dir and the case list disagree, or when a known post bug has a golden.\n- `docs/decisions/926-post-script-suites.md`.\n\nNo product code changed. No new dependency between crates.\n\n## Edge cases (shared by all posts)\n\n| Case | What | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `arcs` | XY ccw + cw, XZ, YZ (split at its Z extremum by the builder), a 2 mm helix | cl, guarded in post |\n| `full_circle` | a ring as the generators write it (two XY halves) | cl, guarded in post |\n| `full_circle_raw` | one 360-degree arc record (a foreign producer could write it) | hand-written, round-trip guard |\n| `drill_retract` | two pecked holes, R plane Z1, hop Z3, clearance Z10 | motion, guarded in app |\n| `tool_change` | T1 facing (M3), then T2 a left-hand thread toward -Z that needs M4 (`PARAM SpindleDirection reverse`) | cl, guarded in post |\n| `rotary` | 3+2 index to A30, a feed that changes the lean to B30, commanded return upright; posted on `tilthead.mch` | cl, guarded in post |\n| `probe` | bore centre, four touches, sets G55 | motion, guarded in app |\n| `empty_section` | a section with no motion | `post::dump` of an empty path, guarded in post |\n| `extreme_coords` | 1 um moves, a 2 um arc, +-9999.999 and 99999.999 mm, F1 and F99999 | cl, guarded in post |\n\n## Golden / refusal matrix\n\n`nc` = program golden, `R` = refusal golden (its named reason), `BUG #n` = known post bug: posted, not compared, no golden.\n\n| Post | arcs | full_circle | full_circle_raw | drill_retract | tool_change | rotary | probe | empty | extreme |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| fanuc | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | BUG #997 | nc | nc | nc |\n| haas | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | R no RTCP | nc | nc | nc |\n| mazak | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | R no RTCP | nc | nc | nc |\n| sinumerik | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | R no RTCP | nc | nc | nc |\n| heidenhain | nc (non-XY arcs chorded) | nc | nc | nc (chain expanded) | R threadHands | R no RTCP | R no probe hooks | nc | nc |\n| tormach | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | R no A about X | nc | nc | nc |\n| doosan-dnm | nc | nc | nc | BUG #994 | R threadHands | R no clamp codes | BUG #995 | nc | nc |\n| carvera | nc | nc | nc | nc (chain expanded) | R threadHands | R 3-axis | R no probe hooks | nc | nc |\n| fanuc-lathe | R milling arcs | R half-turn no lead | R not a thread arc | R off the meridian | nc (M03 -> M04, G32) | R no rotary | R no probe hooks | nc | R off the meridian |\n| tormach-lathe | R milling arcs | R half-turn no lead | R not a thread arc | R off the meridian | nc (M3 -> M4, G33) | R no rotary | R no probe hooks | nc | R off the meridian |\n| tormach-plasma | R rpm | R rpm | R rpm | R rpm + no cycle | R threadHands + rpm | R rpm | R no probe hooks | R rpm | R rpm |\n\nEvery golden was read before committing.\n\n## Post bugs found (filed, not baked into goldens)\n\n- **#994 (P0)** - canned-cycle posts (fanuc, haas, mazak, sinumerik, tormach, doosan-dnm) traverse between holes at the R plane, below the hop the verified path uses. Already visible in the app golden `nc/drill_plate.nc` (R0: rapid X10 -> X30 at Z0).\n- **#995 (P1)** - a probing section starts flood coolant: doosan-dnm always, every mill post on a machine that lists Flood.\n- **#996 (P1)** - the command-line post ignores a vendor `.mch` kinematics tree (no rotaries, spindle limit, coolants reach the script). The runner works around it by passing `post::machine::mirror(parse_mch(..))` for the rotary case; it can pass the file straight through once #996 lands.\n- **#997 (P2)** - fanuc writes `C0` on a machine with no C rotary.\n- **#998 (P2)** - tormach-plasma's machine-less refusal reads \"no machine is not declared a plasma machine\" (kept in the refusal goldens: text only).\n\nObservations not filed (dialect questions I could not check against public docs offline): the mazak post's `MOTON`/`MOTOFF` spindle words, and the sinumerik post's ISO-style `G73`/`G80` cycles in an 840D program.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green (post suites: lib, axis_direction_cli, comp, comp_plane, mch_head_search, post_engine, recorded_streams, the 11 script suites; app recorded_post_streams 2 fns).\n- Pinned by: `script_carvera`, `script_doosan_dnm`, `script_fanuc`, `script_fanuc_lathe`, `script_haas`, `script_heidenhain`, `script_mazak`, `script_sinumerik`, `script_tormach`, `script_tormach_lathe`, `script_tormach_plasma` (9 tests each), `recorded_streams` (10), app `recorded_post_streams` (2).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test recorded_post_streams -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised / left for slice 2\n\n- The ten app tests named in #926's body (`fanuc_post`, `probe_dialects`, `probe_guard`, `probe_report`, `probe_tormach`, `inverted_probe`, `arc_planes`, `inverted_equivalence`, `inverted_post`, `vertical_arc_entry`) are not moved yet. Several of them are edited by the open PRs #967 / #972 (gate maps, file moves), so moving them now would conflict with both; slice 2 should follow those merges. This PR touches none of the files of #967 or #972.\n- Machine variants: only the rotary case posts with a machine; coolant, spindle-limit and travel behaviour per machine are not in the matrix.\n- Post options (`postOptions`, e.g. G76 threading) are not exercised.\n\nEffort: high. Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #926\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
